//
// GEMMA4-E2B Q4NX decode throughput vs KV depth, into gemma4_e2b_q4nx.sweep.json
// (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// Decode-only and synthetic (latency, never correctness -- run_npu2_verify.lit
// is the correctness gate), so unlike the profile test this needs no HF weights
// and no hf_token: the context is set by sizing the KV cache, not by prefilling
// a real prompt of that length.
//
// The counterpart to run_npu2_prefill_sweep.lit (TTFT vs prompt length). Each
// point rebuilds the FULL-DEPTH template pair -- SWEEP_UNI_DEC=35, all 35
// decoder layers. Building fewer would measure a fraction of a dispatch and
// report a number tens of times too good.
//
// EVERY CONTEXT IS IN --expect-fail, AND THAT IS TEMPORARY. Measured on a
// development box (NPU2 Strix, amdxdna 2.23.0), this sweep is completely clean:
//
//     1024 18.21 | 2048 16.27 | 4096 13.39 | 8192 9.91
//    16384  6.52 | 32768  3.87 | 65536  2.14 tok/s, 131072 unreachable
//
// On the nightly runner (amdxdna 2.21.0) the same binaries hang in dispatch
// with ERT_CMD_STATE_TIMEOUT at roughly 10% per decode wave, which compounds to
// ~97% at 35 waves -- issue #1984, where the evidence and the five refuted
// theories are recorded. Retrying cannot rescue a full-depth run. Marking the
// points expected-fail lets this test still build all 35 waves and publish the
// numbers on any host that can produce them, without reddening a nightly for a
// defect that is not in this model's code.
//
// The cost is the guard the sibling sweeps carry: there is no CHECK on a parsed
// tok/s here, so a regression that emptied the curve would not be caught by
// this test. WHEN #1984 IS FIXED, drop --expect-fail and add back a CHECK-NEXT
// on decode_tokens_per_sec; do not leave it in this shape once the dispatch is
// reliable.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, peano_ge22, llvm_link_pre23
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_decode.py --model-name gemma4_e2b_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --template-dir %S --bench-model gemma4-e2b --vocab-chunk-i2 27 --n-layers 35 --contexts 1024,2048,4096,8192,16384,32768,65536,131072 --expect-fail 1024,2048,4096,8192,16384,32768,65536,131072 --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --xrt-dir %XRT_DIR --out gemma4_e2b_q4nx.sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < gemma4_e2b_q4nx.sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "gemma4_e2b_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "context_len"
// CHECK: "context_len": 2048
